# Brewfile.vscode — VS Code extensions, opt-in.
#
#   brew bundle --file=Brewfile.vscode
#
# These used to live in the main Brewfile: 148 extension IDs produced by
# `brew bundle dump`, roughly a third of them abandoned colour themes. They are
# split out here because they are a different kind of thing from packages — they
# are per-editor, they change far more often, and VS Code's built-in Settings
# Sync already carries them between machines. Treat this file as the seed for a
# fresh machine, not as the source of truth.
#
# WHAT WAS DROPPED (all recoverable from git history):
#   - 49 colour/icon themes. Only Dracula is kept, because ghostty and the rest
#     of this repo are themed Dracula. Themes are a one-click reinstall.
#   - 4 duplicates of extensions that are already covered by a sibling here.
#   - 3 that are dead or no longer wanted: Flow, the Sourcegraph extension, and
#     a former-employer extension.
#
# Anything below that looks unused is still here on purpose: it was kept rather
# than guessed at. Prune freely — that is the point of the file being readable.


# ─── Editing, navigation, formatting ─────────────────────────────────────────
